Z||000000||otis||02-28-2000||11:29 PM||||I have read the previous posts on exhaust<BR>upgrades and in particular mufflers. I went<BR>to the muffler  shop to have the flow-<BR>master installed on my 86GT. They could not<BR>do the job without more explanation or<BR>pictures  etc. Does anyone on the list<BR>have pics or explanation of how to  do<BR>this  type of installation on the Fiero.<BR>The mentioned the use of mandrel bent pipe<BR>and fittings. This must be different  from<BR>the usual bending of  pipe done on their<BR>pipe bending machine. Thanks for the help||||reg||5
Z||000001||Shiner||02-28-2000||11:37 PM||||Normal pipe benders cause a reduction in the pipe at the bends.  Mandrel bends do not.  You could run 3" pipe all the way back, but if it is reduced to 2" in any place, for all intents and purposes, it's a 2" exhaust system.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P> I think the way to go would be to get a Borla system.  Not sure if they are doing a second run of the systems or not.  They aren't cheap, but that sucker will outlast the car.||||reg||1
Z||000002||AL||02-28-2000||11:54 PM||||hey otis i haven't got to do it myself yet, but i was thinking of unbolting the exhuast from the cat down and take it to the muffler place with my flowmaster and say,you see that! i want you to make me a new system exactly like this one, except i want this flowmaster installed on the new exhuast you are going to make me, and i want stainless steel please, and that way i don't have to hear there excuses cause they have the original to copy it off.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Bruce||02-28-2000||11:56 PM||||From what I've learned, the flowmaster installation is not worth the hassle or the price for what you get in performance. I'm going to sell my unused flowmaster and install a Walker, or something similar. $.02||||reg||1
